<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hàm Nghi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1871">1871</a>–<a href="/years/1943">1943</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hàm Nghi was emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> of the Nguyễn dynasty from 1884 to 1885. Enthroned at thirteen, he fled the capital Huế in July 1885 with the regent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ton-that-thuyet">Tôn Thất Thuyết</a> after a failed attack on the French, and his name was used to rally the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/can-vuong">Cần Vương</a> resistance movement. Betrayed and captured in 1888, he was exiled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>, where he lived as a painter until his death in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ham-nghi.jpg" alt="Hàm Nghi" width="320" height="452" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vua_H%C3%A0m_Nghi_n%C4%83m_1900.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
